message.content:
This is a leather notebook cover, which CBP has typically classified in heading 4202 as an article of a kind normally carried in the pocket or handbag, or alternatively in 4820 as book covers. Many CBP rulings place refillable leather notebook/journal covers in 4202.92 or 4820.10. Here, the cover holds a removable notebook insert by elastic cords and is not itself a notebook. Heading 4820 covers "binders (other than book covers), folders and file covers", and book covers are included in 4820.50 (albums for samples or collections, book covers). The leather cover is a "book cover" and so falls in 4820.90 "other".

The text of 4820 reads: 4820.10 registers, account books, notebooks, order books, receipt books, letter pads, memorandum pads, diaries and similar articles; 4820.20 exercise books; 4820.30 binders (other than book covers), folders and file covers; 4820.40 manifold business forms; 4820.50 albums for samples or collections; 4820.90 other. Book covers of leather are excluded from chapter 48 only if they are of leather (Note 2 to chapter 42?). In fact, 4202 covers "briefcases, school satchels, spectacle cases... and similar containers", and a leather cover for a notebook is arguably a similar container. CBP rulings on leather refillable journal covers have often held 4202.92.9026 (other, with outer surface of leather), or 4202.31 for items normally carried in pocket or handbag. A notebook cover is likely larger than a wallet, so 4202.91/92 applies. I'll choose 4202.92.9026, "Other: with outer surface of sheeting of plastics or textile materials", which is not correct for leather. For leather, 4202.21 is handbags, 4202.31 is pocket-type articles, and 4202.91 is "other" with leather outer surface. 4202.91.00 has a 10-digit statistical suffix 4202.91.0090. I'll go with the "other" leather subheading.

{"hts_code": "4202.91.0090", "reason": "A leather notebook cover is a container-type case of heading 4202 with an outer surface of leather, so it falls in the 'other' residual provision rather than in heading 4820."}
